      "description": "Presentation House in Dawson Street, the former St Mary's Convent of the Presentation Sisters, Lismore, New South Wales, photographed in August 2024 (Tony Rees photograph). This building, designed in what was termed in a contemporary account \"the Franco-Gothic-Renaissance style of architecture\", by Messrs. Waddell and Denning, of Sydney, was officially opened in 1907 to replace a previous convent building lost in a fire in 1905. The last nuns departed in 2004; following restoration, the building was reopened in 2014 as the premises for the Catholic Schools Office for the Diocese of Lismore.",
